*B 1,Contents
Welcome to the CXL demo.

This program shows what the CXL compatible library can
do. Pick a menu with the arrow keys, its highlighted
letter or the mouse, and press Enter.

  ^File menu^        about the demo, leaving it
  ^Windows menu^     overlapping and moving windows
  ^Data menu^        forms, pick lists and colours

Tab moves between the topics above, Enter opens one.
PgDn shows the next page of a topic, Esc closes help.
*P
How help works

Help comes from CXLDEMO.HLP, a plain text file next
to the program. Each topic starts with a line
"*B number,name" and ends with "*E". A "*P" line
starts a new page, and a name between carets is a
cross-reference to another topic.

The program sets the topic as the menu bar moves, so
F1 always explains what is under the bar.

Back to the ^Contents^.
*E
*B 2,File menu
The File menu

About...    shows the library version and screen size.
BIOS date   reads the date stamped in the BIOS.
Exit        leaves the demo. Alt-X does too, from
            anywhere in the menus.

Back to the ^Contents^.
*E
*B 3,Windows menu
The Windows menu

Overlap        opens four windows, one over another,
               then brings each to the top in turn.
               Text written to a covered window
               stays underneath until it is raised.
Move and size  moves a window with the arrow keys
               and resizes it with + and -.
Hide and show  hides a window and brings it back.

Every window keeps a copy of the screen under it, and
casts a shadow onto whatever lies behind.

Back to the ^Contents^.
*E
*B 4,Data menu
The Data menu

Address form   a data entry form; see ^Forms^.
Pick a fruit   chooses a string from a list.
Pick a file    chooses a file in the current directory.
Colours        chooses a text colour.

Back to the ^Contents^.
*E
*B 5,Forms
Filling in the form

Type in each field. The format of a field decides what
it accepts: names are capitalised, the state is upper
case and the zip code takes only digits.

  Enter, Tab      next field
  Shift-Tab       previous field
  Home, End       start or end of the field
  Ins             insert or overtype
  Ctrl-Enter      finish the form
  Esc             cancel the form

Back to the ^Contents^.
*E
*B 6,Pick lists
Pick lists

Move the bar with the arrow keys, PgUp and PgDn, or
press the first letter of an entry to jump to it.
Enter picks the entry under the bar, Esc cancels.

Back to the ^Contents^.
*E
*B 7,Colours
Choosing a colour

The arrow keys change the foreground and background
colours. The sample shows the result. Enter picks it,
Esc keeps the old colour.

Back to the ^Contents^.
*E
